+# Glossary
+
+- **Plan change**: moving a live subscription to another plan and/or interval with
+  `BillingService.change_plan`. Its target is always a full (plan, interval) pair.
+- **Upgrade**: a plan change to a plan with a higher `monthly_price` than the current plan,
+  whatever interval is involved. Takes effect immediately and is prorated.
+- **Downgrade**: a plan change to a plan with a lower `monthly_price`. Scheduled for the end of
+  the current period.
+- **Lateral change**: a plan change to a different plan with the same `monthly_price`. Treated
+  like a downgrade (scheduled).
+- **Interval switch**: changing between monthly and annual billing. Always scheduled for the end
+  of the current period, in either direction; there are no refunds for unused annual time.
+- **Scheduled change**: the (plan, interval) a subscription moves to at its next renewal. It
+  hasn't happened yet, so prorations still use the current plan. A new request replaces it; an
+  upgrade or a cancel discards it.
+- **Proration**: on an upgrade, crediting the current plan and charging the new plan for the
+  remaining days of the period, at current-interval prices. Each of the two lines is
+  `price × remaining_days / period_days` and is rounded half up on its own.
+- **Remaining days / period days**: `period_end − today` and `period_end − period_start` of the
+  current, half-open period.
